[{"id":"VRCE-1-39-1","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":39,"verse":1,"english":"Hearing the speech of the celestials, that possessor of the six attributes, the Grand-sire, spoke to them exceedingly frightened and deprived of their senses on beholding the prowess of Sagara's sons like to the Destroyer himself.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-40-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1039001","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1f08ba0a85b464e048c8c627a629d51a44c520a5705c5112d2932d7089c34405","compact":"df55e94ed982ac52b3a94e1c6130f92b7bc1b3405735c8772a0dc2f4f754c71a","nasal":"b6d8be30c572d43617a2e870cdd4af157b5cc80002c93d2e959d3cc4ca16b058"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-39-2","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":39,"verse":2,"english":"This entire Earth belong to the intelligent Vasudeva, she being his consort. And that adorable one is indeed her lord. And assuming the form of Kapila, he unceasingly sustain the Earth. And the sons of king Sagara will be consumed by the fire of his wrath.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.9,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-40-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1039002","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"481c09bf4edae02626ce348d81466229a0fc5ea2ff06ae139580c688d620bb42","compact":"7eb3897bd25c7768a4c8ccc9240d9b7fad16e1991dacc07f89fb0cd2ccbf9a35","nasal":"7eb3897bd25c7768a4c8ccc9240d9b7fad16e1991dacc07f89fb0cd2ccbf9a35"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-39-3","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":39,"verse":3,"english":"The pre-ordained excavation of the Earth, as well as the testruction of Sagara's sons, had been foreseen by the farsighted.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-40-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1039003","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7a6b6454d17e83906ec001623be05f30cf093374f73c72a1db8d2ea846d7a780","compact":"658ebdafc63d94c04a0e1d1c284870eb0127b9ec5f2dd05053e8e844f152d279","nasal":"658ebdafc63d94c04a0e1d1c284870eb0127b9ec5f2dd05053e8e844f152d279"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-39-4","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":39,"verse":4,"english":"Hearing the words of the Grand-sire. those repressors of their foes, the three and thirty* celestials, being exceedingly rejoiced, went back to their respective quarters. *The eight Vasus, eleven Rudras, twelve Adityas and two Asvins.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.892,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-40-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1039004","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"eac7d295315b09881bca0114612422a58aa562a7dcbb56b36decc5739ce3a65c","compact":"60afd46795fa7d9d3e3a01c1ffb312fb582a7cadae9eb6000b8caab5db398741","nasal":"60afd46795fa7d9d3e3a01c1ffb312fb582a7cadae9eb6000b8caab5db398741"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-39-5","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":39,"verse":5,"english":"And as the sons of Sagara were riving the Earth, there arose a mighty noise, like to the bursting of thunder.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.794,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-40-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1039005","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"733bfc9eafa3163a5e4dafee0a7313103fd41c83ea768d263acd91a80db12ef0","compact":"c5eebac9d1fc3562b7fc550e9e58e721757ed99cf766ac9a23449f1897fa4bd9","nasal":"e6d4149c134eaac2573e8fe9d3682a6e40abcfc7d689ad34248beae3e2828fd2"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-39-6","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":39,"verse":6,"english":"Then, having rived the entire Earth and ranged it all around, the sons, of Sagara together (returned to their father) and spoke to him.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.899,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-40-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1039006","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"905315c3872e63bd59a676ae152fac2664b91205d6bf2cddd8172c3f1624e3ad","compact":"c870a3f424c4f6ab36f640e5b65214b1b35ccee3c5a34ddccd7df098a588c8d9","nasal":"c870a3f424c4f6ab36f640e5b65214b1b35ccee3c5a34ddccd7df098a588c8d9"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-39-7","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":39,"verse":7,"english":"By us has the Earth been extensively surveyed, and have powerful deities and Dānavas. Rākşasas, Piśācas, Uragas and Pannagas been slain; and yet do we find neither the horse nor the stealer thereof. What are we to do now? Good betide you, do you consider it well.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.887,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-40-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1039007","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5a843145c0b791d78b2638cb6db702a35c9b25fadb1c385546835f2190dae09a","compact":"f20e2013fbeb9627ce90d282bf33600a29745ee50a989d1bf3e10576a7c923b7","nasal":"666ed510c0b009c8574f61d4e283811d9bacfeba18d87785c79cf2b8de171d4a"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-39-8","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":39,"verse":8,"english":"By us has the Earth been extensively surveyed, and have powerful deities and Dānavas. Rākşasas, Piśācas, Uragas and Pannagas been slain; and yet do we find neither the horse nor the stealer thereof. What are we to do now? Good betide you, do you consider it well.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.869,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-40-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1039008","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fa751b93922c1ca07ffd1d7c3fc6c61de2459e04dc0e14f94692f5f819837429",