 N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6ca0ad6add6ecaa1adc58b1d76a921e29ad87c3c4aca8c15026ae0fb2327ec5e","compact":"951f7ccf91cc064831c4dd6badade6fc57f0ce49eae3675efb1e9036b94e71ee","nasal":"27c990742aaf7e3a24802ffc546a23a33592cea16ec77b6e94c8e565d4c14385"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-39-15","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":39,"verse":15,"english":"Thereupon, O Rāma, going round that mighty elephant, and honouring him duly, they went on piercing the under earth.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.938,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-40-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1039015","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bd787d285f9cc2e03e5ee8123732dbb09ec21f32a1802cbe18dfa5c9625213b9","compact":"60ce4876997771ce320181f0ff40538af30eb8c60cb9d101ce462a0d5ba8d08f","nasal":"9d1c92f9e2ba70422e4ce1098cd35aafa4dab800a0360d5c7865e299c14ed37f"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-39-16","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":39,"verse":16,"english":"And having pierced the East, they pierced the South, and in the Southern quarter also they beheld a mighty elephant, the high-souled Mahāpadma, resembling a huge hill, holding the earth on his head. And thereat they marvelled greatly.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-40-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1039016","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5bded344345132b36ea3ead2ea9e7f2cccab69cfa3a9391cd53aa5cec2df8936","compact":"f9643c45315c459965b89791508267668395f58f154d2b0f6d2e2a9e68cbfa1b","nasal":"f9643c45315c459965b89791508267668395f58f154d2b0f6d2e2a9e68cbfa1b"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-39-17","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":39,"verse":17,"english":"And having pierced the East, they pierced the South, and in the Southern quarter also they beheld a mighty elephant, the high-souled Mahāpadma, resembling 