,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":39,"verse":20,"english":"And having gone round him and asked him as to his welfare, they delving on, arrived at the Northern region.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.831,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-40-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1039020","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9033a8b2256f9ccb73378776d04a30512f5e9b0d5662cb7f4f52806b59cc8011","compact":"73f1d44fe242b045b2999f4579341cb2316968864706bcbe4c5e9b971e710464","nasal":"0a196b745f25e94d1965938859fcbc606fe40df1b383e5820479b27d658e351a"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-39-21","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":39,"verse":21,"english":"And on the North like wise, O foremost of the Raghus, they beheld Bhadra, white as snow, holding this earth on his goodly person.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-40-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1039021","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"77618894676d51b5bd96e79ceaf48972f60d33392dbbfa7a60b00e6986074486","compact":"d4422bfd7cd7f993bf32ba69a0ff36b0b6558cd5b0ea4924545cbb90b47667bc","nasal":"938016fc46ccf6a0b5c1e4b70c4faf3ac8f68dc2da2b013b8c6748af06a4fd79"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-39-22","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":39,"verse":22,"english":"Having felt as well as gone round him, those sixty thousand sons of Sagara went on penetrating the depths of the earth.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.877,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-40-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1039022","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"33d038a92e79e6ca86e273485c622f78320bcfa4211845ac8ca704e933c3bcbf","compact":"16bc07c4291de3592d4ae72b4c4417aec208c846509f73c1348f75cbb4dcd712","nasal":"16bc07c4291de3592d4ae72b4c4417aec20